A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate when the **failure cause matches**, not merely its subject
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), superseding decision 0001):

1. Read the body and identify the affected product, tenant and entry path.
2. Look up the tenant's locale and booking form. For #4471, use the exported cause classifier.
3. Find an open ticket for that cause; subject matches are candidates only.
4. Merge only when the cause matches. Otherwise open a separate issue or investigate missing evidence.
5. Count distinct report IDs, not rows in overlapping export pages.

<Callout>
The same tenant and subject can cover both a parser failure and a form-hint failure.
Browser locale and intake tags are guesses, not evidence of the tenant's actual configuration.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the report separate while you investigate. Unknown tenants and bodies inconsistent with
the assigned cause need follow-up, not an automatic merge. See the
[#4471 review](/kb/incidents/4471-review) for the evidence and unusual date-shift observations.
